From 8914c58a9070dd4ea2b466668afe6f6ce3938f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:58:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 533/533] feat(desktop): instant session opens from a local
 transcript cache [daveey]

A click painted at most a 40-message localStorage tail for 50 sessions, and a
remote open waited 2.6-8 s on SSH before anything fresh. Now:

- Electron main keeps a SQLite transcript cache (node:sqlite, userData/
  transcript-cache.sqlite): raw /messages rows keyed by (connection, profile,
  stored id), the latest 200 plus older pages the user loaded; LRU 1000
  sessions / 256 MiB, 8 MiB per entry. The renderer reads it with a sync IPC so
  the click paints in the same tick.
- A background prefetcher reads the local hermes-hub replica and keeps the 200
  most recently active session tips per registry gateway (people's chats before
  automations) current, refetching when activity or message_count moves.
- resumeSession paints the cache, starts the REST read at the click when the
  row hands over its owner (reused by the cold path, so one read), and
  reconciles without re-rendering an unchanged transcript.
- A row whose gateway is unreachable opens read-only from the cache; a send
  shows the asleep notice and keeps the draft.
- [open-timing] log line per open: click -> first paint -> stages -> reconciled.
- The gateway switch no longer wipes the (now connection-scoped) cache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
